\par                                       UHX-13
\par                       RULES FOR THE DESIGN OF FIXED TUBESHEETS
\par                       ----------------------------------------
\par          Program name: * AsmeVip * Pressure Vessels & Heat Exchangers *   Vers. 5.18
\par \pard\plain \s18\qc\widctlpar\tx4536 \f2\fs18\lang1040       ASME VIII Div.1 2004 Ed. A06      \par \pard\plain \s18\qj\widctlpar\tx4536 \f2\fs18\lang1040 
\par          FBM Job N{\super 0} UHXm20p2p1  Item                                 Dwg N{\super 0} $         
\par                                 Customer   ________               Designer LP      
\par 
   Calculation Procedure for tubesheets flanged channel-side per sketch UHX-13.1(b)\par
\par 
                                  INPUT DATA\par
                                  ==========\par
\par 
  TubeSheet Id: TubeSheet                 TubeSheet material: TS mat'l            \par
  Shell     Id: Mantello                  Shell     material: TS mat'l            \par
  Tubes     Id: Exchanger tubes           Tube      material: Tube mat'l          \par
  Shell adj.Id: Virola adiacente          Shell adj.material: Shell mat'l         \par 
\par 
  Type of exchanger: Fixed TubeSheets     TubeSheet Support: Flanged channel-side \par
  Number of load conditions   1           TubeSheets of differing thicknesses  NO \par
  Design under differential pressure:  NO \par
\par 
  Inside Diameter of Shell     883   [mm]   Inside Diameter of Channel       0   [mm]\par
  Shell thickness                6   [mm]   Channel thickness                0   [mm]\par
  Shell side corrosion           0   [mm]   Channel side corrosion           0   [mm]\par
  Equivalent Diam for shear       0  [mm]   Tube spacing  (Triangular)     31,75 [mm]\par
  Outside diameter of tubes     25,4 [mm]   Tube thickness                  2,11 [mm]\par
  Number of Tubes in Shell    649    [--]   Tube length                   4267,2 [mm]\par
  Inside Dia of Expans.J.     978    [mm]   Corrosion of Expansion J.          0 [mm]\par
  TubeSheet   Grooves Depth       0  [mm]   TubeSheet   Nom.Thickness      44,5  [mm]\par
  Tube expansion depth          95  [%]\par
  Type of tube-to-T.S. joint    Saldato a>=1.4t               \par
  Factors according App.A       fr:  0,8  fe: N.A.  fy: N.A.\par
  Equivalent Unsupported Buckling Lenght of Tubes                         1498,6 [mm]\par
  Design under vacuum:    shell-side NO     tube-side                            NO \par
  Calculation of Radial Differential Thermal Expansion at the TS required : YES
\par 
      Note: A null Inside Dia of Expans. Joint indicates the absence of the same\par
      Note: Shell adj. is the course attached to the TS, possibly having differing thk.\par 
            The said course is    30  [mm] thick and   305  [mm] long. 
\par 
      Load Cond. nb.  1: Design Condition        \par
\par 
                          SOURCES FOR PHYSICAL DATA\par
\par 
                Elastic Modulus                       Thermal Expansion\par
  TubeSheet : not defined (manual entry)            \par
  Shell     : not defined (manual entry)            not defined (manual entry)            \par
  Tubes     : not defined (manual entry)            not defined (manual entry)            \par
